From d8fa66648f07c65ffb9b44e4889659610110b084 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: folia-mobile <mobile@folia.local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:31:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/97] fix(mobile): keep one upcoming lyric line, and let the
 wall tools panel scroll

Two shell-only UI corrections, both measured off a 2048x930 screenshot rather
than guessed.

The upcoming-lyric preview measured 298x122 CSS px, which is exactly two lines
plus the -inset-x-10/-inset-y-6 blurred backing. It is not positioned badly: the
subtitle baseline sits 112px above the screen bottom and the bottom bar's top
edge is at 121px, so it already hugs the bar. What put it in the middle of the
picture is its own 122px height on a ~465px-tall landscape viewport. So the fix
is to show only the nearest line and drop the backing, not to move it.

The wall tools panel was flex:none with overflow:hidden, so on a short viewport
it grew taller than the space above it and was clipped at the top edge with no
way to reach the rest. It now shrinks (with a 120px floor) and scrolls. Lattice
shares the component, so it is fixed there too.

Desktop builds keep upstream's appearance.
